// Judge validation subset. Hand-label 30-50 items from ONE run, then:
//     rag-evals validate-judge --run-id <run_id>
//
// Procedure used (keep it identical if you extend this file, or the agreement
// number stops meaning anything):
//   1. Run a config with generation enabled. Do NOT read the judge's verdict yet.
//   2. For each sampled qid, open results/<run_id>.json and read only the
//      question, the retrieved passages, and the system answer.
//   3. Label:
//        grounded  - is EVERY claim in the answer supported by those passages?
//                    (judge the passages only; ignore whether it is true)
//                    an abstention asserts nothing, so it is grounded
//        correct   - does it match the reference answer in substance?
//                    an abstention on an answerable question is not correct
//        abstained - did it decline, rather than hedge while still asserting?
//   4. Only then compare against the judge, and record why you differed in `note`.
//
// Labels are pinned to run_id because a label is only valid for the answer text
// it was written against. Re-label when the answers change.
//
// Schema:
// {"qid":"q001","run_id":"008-retrieval-hybrid","grounded":true,"correct":true,"abstained":false,"note":""}
//
// Current contents: 40 items labelled against 008-retrieval-hybrid on 2026-09-05
// (17 fact, 12 negative, 6 multi-hop, 5 near-miss), blind to the judge.
